# Frontend Conventions

## Page structure

Every page in `app/javascript/pages/` uses `export default function <FileName>` (matching the file,
not the route) with a props interface declared **in the same file**. Props are **snake_case**,
mirroring Rails serialization:

```tsx
interface RoiProps {
  monthly_trends: Array<{ month: string; sent: number }>
  can_edit_metrics: boolean
  errors?: Record<string, string[]>
}

export default function Index({ monthly_trends, can_edit_metrics }: RoiProps) {
```

## Layouts are wrapper components, NOT Inertia's `Layout` static property

The `page.default.layout` hook is deliberately commented out in
[app/javascript/entrypoints/inertia.ts](app/javascript/entrypoints/inertia.ts). Each page wraps its
own JSX. Never write `Page.layout = ...`.

```tsx
return (
  <AuthenticatedLayout title={t('roi.title')} account={account} organization={organization} flash={flash}>
```

`AuthenticatedLayout` requires `title`, `account`, `children`. `SettingsLayout` instead reads
`auth`/`flash` itself and takes `currentTab` + `sidebarSections`.

Shared Inertia props come from `usePage<SharedProps>().props` — the `[key: string]: unknown` index
signature is required by Inertia's generic.

## Imports: relative only

**There are no path aliases.** `@/lib/i18n` does not resolve (the docblock in `lib/i18n.ts` claiming
otherwise is wrong). Use relative paths: `import { t } from '../../lib/i18n'`.
The `components/ui/index.ts` and `layouts/index.ts` barrels exist but are not imported from in
practice — import directly from the component file to match surrounding code.

## i18n — never hard-code user-facing strings

```tsx
t('customer_settings.team.table.name')                          // snake_case, dot-separated
t('customer_settings.team.members_of', { organization: name })  // interpolation -> %{organization}
t('roi.metrics.across_months', { count: months })               // pluralization -> one:/other:
t(`admin.users.statuses.${user.status}`)                        // dynamic key, static prefix
```

Add keys to `config/locales/en.yml` (plus other locales), then export to the frontend:

```bash
mise exec -- i18n export --config config/i18n-js.yml
```

## Forms

Prefer Inertia's `useForm`; surface errors via the `error` prop on `Input`:

```tsx
const { data, setData, post, processing, errors } = useForm({ email: '' })
<Input label={t('...')} value={data.email} onChange={e => setData('email', e.target.value)} error={errors.email} />
<Button type="submit" loading={processing}>{t('common.save')}</Button>
```

Raw `fetch` is used in a few places for non-navigational mutations and must send
`'X-CSRF-Token'`. Reach for `router.post/patch` + `useForm` first.

## Toasts

Prefer the local wrapper over importing `sonner` directly (`Toaster.tsx` re-exports `toast`):

```tsx
import { toast } from '../../components/ui/Toaster'
toast.success(flash.notice)
toast.error(t('admin.common.error'))
```

## Icons

Always `lucide-react` — never inline SVG. Size with classes (`size-4`, or `h-4 w-4`):

```tsx
import { Inbox, LogOut } from 'lucide-react'
<LogOut className="size-4" />
```

## Sidebar navigation

Customer nav lives in `CUSTOMER_NAV_ITEMS` in
[app/javascript/layouts/AuthenticatedLayout.tsx](app/javascript/layouts/AuthenticatedLayout.tsx):
`{ id, label, icon, href }`. Add new top-level entries there.

## After changes

```bash
npm run check
```
